/-!
# Native octad reductions for K.4.3 and K.4.4

The range of an octad-kernel involution's displacement is its actual Vz as
soon as H.16.2(6) supplies dimension four. Quadratic actors on the code or
its dual therefore lie in the actual pointwise centralizer Dz. Comparing
the native fixed dimension four for four-subgroups of KO with H.16.2(7)
proves Dz ∩ KO = <z>. Pairs generated by z and an element of Dz are quadratic,
and their commutator is the sum of the two actual displacement images.

For the literal setwise pair stabilizer {0,9}, every noncyclic elementary
actor contains an inner involution. Its retained displacement puts the
restricted actor in Dz without lifting restricted quadraticity to U. Its
fixed octad contains both marked points. A point-stabilizer bound in Dz then
gives rank two and the ambient fixed six-space by orbit-stabilizer and
H.16.2(7). The remaining pair-span calculation supplies the cocode consumer.

The dimension, elementary-abelian and fixed-space formula hypotheses below
are precisely the relevant earlier H.16.2(6)--(7) conclusions. The additional
point-stabilizer and displacement-span premises in the final reductions
remain separate K.4 geometry obligations. No intersection of two Dz groups,
conjugacy of quadratic subgroups, or six-space conclusion is assumed as an
earlier Chapter H result.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), H.16.2,
printed pp.402--403; K.4.3--4, printed pp.458--459, refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/

public section

open Representation Representation.BinaryOffender
open Sporadic.Mathieu Sporadic.Mathieu.M24LocalGeometry
open CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterH.Section13To16
open scoped IsMulCommutative Pointwise
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterK.Mathieu.OctadGeometry
